Vita owns one GL/GXM context on the main thread and selects Aurora Inline mode.
In that existing serialized mode only, avoid the worker mutex/atomic notifications
when processing or clearing the FIFO. Keep the original bytes, processing order,
draw-done callbacks, watermarks, range assertions and all Thread/Drain locking.
No game tick, actor update or command is skipped. Calls from another producer
thread are not supported by the existing Inline graphics context contract.

